response.value:
We’ll recreate the prototype as a React screen: black background, floating Otto, neon speech bubble, typewriter dialogue, tap-to-continue, then a ticket-number field. The prototype also asks for a cultivator name, but your updated plan needs **only the ticket number**.

Let’s do one step: build and display that landing screen. **Ticket validation and the transition into the story will come next.** To avoid showing an unvalidated “ENTER” button, the button in this step will stay disabled until we wire up validation.

### 1. Copy Otto into the React app’s public images

In VS Code’s Explorer, copy the existing `otto.png` from the repository root into `game/public/images/`. The copied file should be at:

```text
game/public/images/otto.png
```

### 2. Create the landing screen component

Create `game/src/components/WelcomeScreen.jsx` and paste in:

```jsx
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react'
import './WelcomeScreen.css'

const dialogueLines = [
  'Welcome Miss Hunter to Wang Chuan Tech Pte. Ltd.!',
  "I am OTTO-MENGPO, your guide for today's VR experience.",
  'Today we will visit the Spirit Realm and lend a hand to some troubled spirits!',
  'Are you ready?',
]

function WelcomeScreen() {
  const [lineIndex, setLineIndex] = useState(0)
  const [visibleText, setVisibleText] = useState('')
  const [ticketNumber, setTicketNumber] = useState('')

  const currentLine = dialogueLines[lineIndex]
  const isLastLine = lineIndex === dialogueLines.length - 1
  const spielComplete = isLastLine && visibleText === currentLine

  useEffect(() => {
    if (visibleText.length >= currentLine.length) {
      return undefined
    }

    const timer = window.setTimeout(() => {
      setVisibleText(currentLine.slice(0, visibleText.length + 1))
    }, 50)

    return () => window.clearTimeout(timer)
  }, [currentLine, visibleText])

  function handleAdvance() {
    if (visibleText !== currentLine) {
      setVisibleText(currentLine)
      return
    }

    if (!isLastLine) {
      setLineIndex((index) => index + 1)
      setVisibleText('')
    }
  }

  return (
    <main className="welcome-page">
      <div className="welcome-content">
        <button
          className="welcome-advance"
          type="button"
          onClick={handleAdvance}
          disabled={spielComplete}
          aria-label="Tap to continue Otto's introduction"
        >
          <img
            className="welcome-otto"
            src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/otto.png`}
            alt="Otto, your guide"
          />

          <span className="welcome-bubble">
            <span className="welcome-dialogue" aria-live="polite">
              {visibleText}
            </span>
          </span>
        </button>

        {!spielComplete && visibleText === currentLine && (
          <p className="welcome-tap-prompt">▼ Tap to continue</p>
        )}

        {spielComplete && (
          <form className="welcome-ticket-form">
            <label className="sr-only" htmlFor="ticket-number">
              Ticket number
            </label>
            <input
              id="ticket-number"
              className="welcome-input"
              type="text"
              placeholder="Your Ticket Number"
              autoComplete="off"
              value={ticketNumber}
              onChange={(event) => setTicketNumber(event.target.value)}
            />
            <button className="welcome-enter" type="button" disabled>
              ENTER
            </button>
            <p className="welcome-hint">
              Ticket entry will be enabled in the next step.
            </p>
          </form>
        )}
      </div>
    </main>
  )
}

export default WelcomeScreen
```

