response.value:
I found the cause: in [WelcomeScreen.css](/workspaces/NFC-Hunt/game/src/components/WelcomeScreen.css), `.welcome-tap-prompt` has `margin: -3.5rem 0 0;`. That large negative top margin pulls it up over the textbox.

Replace the entire `.welcome-tap-prompt` rule with:

```css
.welcome-tap-prompt {
  margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  min-height: 1.5em;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  color: #00f3ff;
  font-size: clamp(9px, 2.2vw, 11px);
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-shadow: 0 0 0.35em rgb(0 243 255 / 80%);
  animation: welcome-pulse 1.5s ease-in-out infinite;
}
```

The `0.5rem` top margin gives it a small gap below the textbox. The prompt stays centered under the textbox because it’s inside `.welcome-bubble-group`. If you want it closer or farther away, adjust only `0.5rem`.

